   - FeatureProvider

2. Added Suspense wrapper with a loading fallback for handling dynamic imports

3. Added an ErrorBoundary component to catch and display any rendering errors

4. Added necessary imports for all the providers

5. Created a QueryClient instance with some sensible defaults

This should resolve the module fetching error by providing all the required context providers that the component needs. The ErrorBoundary will also help catch and display any other rendering errors that might occur.

The providers are added in the same order as they appear in the component stack trace to maintain the correct context hierarchy. The Suspense component will handle the loading state while the dynamic import is being resolved.

